in grand rapids michigan the federal  trial of four militia members charged in  what prosecutors said was a plot to  kidnap michigan governor gretchen  whitmer ended in two acquittals and a  hung jury for two others adriana diaz  reports on this significant defeat for  the federal government in a case that  was a centerpiece of their heavy focus  on domestic terrorism  prosecutors failed to convince the  entire jury that the men were guilty  brandon caserta and dan harris the only  defendant to take the stand were found  not guilty the jury was deadlocked on  all counts for adam fox and barry croft  jr prosecutors painted them as the  ringleaders hell bent on enacting a  second civil war but the defense said  the real masterminds were fbi informants  who they say encouraged the kidnapping  conversations i think what the fbi did  is unconscionable and i think the jury  just sent them a message loud and clear  that these tactics are not going to be  you know  we're not going to condone what they've  done here the government's kidnapping  and weapons charges centered around an  alleged plan to grab governor gretchen  whitmer from her vacation home strand  her on a boat on lake michigan and blow  up a nearby bridge to impede law  enforcement some of the men met at open  carry protests at the state capitol in  2020 rallying against michigan's covet  19 restrictions they spent much of the  summer of 2020 complaining training with  guns and drinking and smoking alongside  the confidential informants  those meetings resulted in thousands of  hours of video and audio evidence  including when croft declared a team  should be ready for a precise quick grab  whitmer whitmer michigan whitmer  at trial the defense said the case was  smoke and mirrors created by those paid  informants who befriended the defendants  paying for meals even driving them  across state lines to attend meetings  after the verdict governor whitmer's  office demanded accountability calling  the alleged plot the result of violent  divisive rhetoric that is all too common  across our country fox and croft could  face a retrial the other defendants walk  free for cbs saturday morning i'm  adriana diaz
 

